  "headline": "Payrolls nearly triple the forecast and chips bounce \u2014 but the S&P still loses 2.7% on the week",
  "standfirst": "October payrolls rose 165,000 against about 59,000 expected and unemployment fell to 4.1%, pushing the two-year yield up and December hike odds back toward 78%. The Nasdaq rose 1.09% as chips won back part of Thursday's crash, with AMD up 11.04%, but the Dow fell 0.46% and most stocks fell. For the week the S&P lost 2.68% and the Nasdaq 3.37%, while WTI fell 13.23% and gold rose 5.02%. The book is flat; Q4 is +34.64 realised, heat 0R.",
